  <constraints>
    <constraint type="cost">For a typical brownfield project with 200 articles: Voyage AI embeddings ~$0.02, Memgraph upserts $0 (local), S3 sync negligible. Combined with Story 6.1 (~$0.50-2.00), full bootstrap pipeline costs ~$0.52-2.05 per project.</constraint>
    <constraint type="verification">Verification queries are non-blocking: if any check fails, emit a warning event but do NOT fail the pipeline. Log which checks failed for manual investigation. This prevents re-running the entire expensive pipeline for minor discrepancies.</constraint>
    <constraint type="infrastructure">Memgraph memory limit is 512MB on t4g.small (2GB RAM total). For 200 articles with 1024-dim embeddings, memory usage should be well within limits. Monitor docker stats during full resync.</constraint>
    <constraint type="architecture">Wiki markdown files are the source of truth. Memgraph is a disposable query accelerator rebuilt from wiki content at any time. Data loss in Memgraph is recoverable (re-run graph-sync) but costly (re-embedding via Voyage AI).</constraint>
    <constraint type="incremental-sync">After full resync, .mycelium/compile-state.json must be updated with content hashes for ALL articles. This enables future incremental syncs to only process changed articles, avoiding re-embedding the entire wiki.</constraint>
    <constraint type="registry-update">The ProjectRegistry type in functions/shared/types/project-registry.ts must be extended with the optional knowledgeGraph field before the DynamoDB update can be type-safe.</constraint>
  </constraints>

